gned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{4}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{4}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}([\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 28\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512933 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162096 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e91708c9-67e2-5228-84fd-1f4ea60064ac" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean-Deviation Form of an Observation Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44e9ff8e-9005-5662-92b6-2423d657e0b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512242} {:answer/id #uuid "4a84cf80-9ac6-550c-9cf0-410296323c5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512257} {:answer/id #uuid "748097f9-a18e-56b6-8d3d-fbd3e7580604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512374} {:answer/id #uuid "fbb61e4f-bff1-5ded-88cc-c64443477ea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512707} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe7ebd9-1482-50a1-accc-9e0e26fccee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "748097f9-a18e-56b6-8d3d-fbd3e7580604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512374} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e40b0a9-1361-5dd4-aab2-b04b18adc043" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1c1c9b0-94ce-5a76-9444-4ee707ea7768" :question/math-academy-id "q-138607" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512887 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162096 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e91708c9-67e2-5228-84fd-1f4ea60064ac" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean-Deviation Form of an Observation Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d61031c-4423-50f9-9efb-1452f6b1952b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512232} {:answer/id #uuid "81c17eac-92ca-59f1-b6be-d25f5b5973a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512402} {:answer/id #uuid "89d6aeda-7054-5e32-a74a-0e2ca343b3d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512421} {:answer/id #uuid "a389c464-59e1-5313-a31f-2255742146be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512483} {:answer/id #uuid "c48aab5b-9b99-510a-a4db-cb8c07a9b5a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c48aab5b-9b99-510a-a4db-cb8c07a9b5a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512572} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cd35d7c-3dff-56b6-ae44-55a4d6ea096b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "52c2be5d-881c-537a-9b60-cd461ebff8ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-138609" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}11 & 13 & 15 \\\\ 10 & 7 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}39 \\\\ 21\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162096 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e91708c9-67e2-5228-84fd-1f4ea60064ac" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean-Deviation Form of an Observation Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b23785e-59c3-5c8b-a7cc-6a257ed32da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512200} {:answer/id #uuid "4e971735-2555-5c2e-bdb4-f467bf99cf12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512272} {:answer/id #uuid "631442a5-3529-5b28-b80d-ea82910b12bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512334} {:answer/id #uuid "baee0313-3aa9-58bc-a651-9d7d64343bda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512547} {:answer/id #uuid "e2da0a70-ad5b-56e8-a291-1aa3b5630162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b23785e-59c3-5c8b-a7cc-6a257ed32da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512200} :answer-field/id #uuid "a34b484a-c298-5baa-a88b-4834839a72f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a6f656ec-c43b-57fd-ba21-5aa8a0f97292" :question/math-academy-id "q-138610" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}21 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162096 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e91708c9-67e2-5228-84fd-1f4ea60064ac" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean-Deviation Form of an Observation Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "801331b6-d1a4-5072-8af1-2b93b2ebefc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512401} {:answer/id #uuid "86f71e12-ebbe-5491-b113-0c7da13d21c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512411} {:answer/id #uuid "c81e532d-af9a-57e2-b63d-acd0722b13be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512583} {:answer/id #uuid "ed76a43b-1de2-586d-a13a-82bab00dc68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512674} {:answer/id #uuid "fc97fbb2-6b7d-542c-ad48-76d5092ef42c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c81e532d-af9a-57e2-b63d-acd0722b13be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512583} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c612bcd-820c-5cdc-80d7-637ac5af81c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fd960ab2-8677-5176-9a5c-025cfe279786" :question/math-academy-id "q-138613" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}15 & 23 & 16 \\\\ 14 & 20 & 20\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}23 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}23 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}54 \\\\ 54\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}23 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512872 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162095 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc84d72a-b9f3-5f99-aa23-31cfe6910d49" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fd9255b-f615-5d83-92d9-2bc78b91998e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}30 & 15 \\\\ 15 & 26\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512130} {:answer/id #uuid "79759a38-a235-5771-92d6-228d11800351" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}37 & -87 \\\\ -87 & 14\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512387} {:answer/id #uuid "90c22079-4b59-5228-be34-e7bd06a853b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512442} {:answer/id #uuid "bf7bf3b9-12f7-5121-8c02-4ec81b6cd692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 27 \\\\ 27 & 34\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512560} {:answer/id #uuid "f26c8ed4-8447-5837-bfea-0aa85c183599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}11 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 34\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fd9255b-f615-5d83-92d9-2bc78b91998e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}30 & 15 \\\\ 15 & 26\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512130} :answer-field/id #uuid "a45e3436-de97-54f9-a787-6f9a2b4c2e98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512812}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "11c41377-dcf0-57a2-b4f3-049053a2f2ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-138628" :question/problem "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $B$ in the mean-deviation form above, where the individual observations are given in columns. \nFind the sample covariance matrix of the data." :question/worked-solution "Recall that  the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{n-1}B{B}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{4-1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}30 & 15 \\\\ 15 & 26\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512893 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162095 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc84d72a-b9f3-5f99-aa23-31cfe6910d49" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "221e06ea-f68c-51ef-b279-1b5f659de9d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 18\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512172} {:answer/id #uuid "4a37a48b-8c5c-5ce1-8b9b-361377f41e19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512256} {:answer/id #uuid "8e900ee1-3dca-5910-b252-b7b9299af900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 18\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512433} {:answer/id #uuid "99853a00-52f1-50b5-8ddd-c3bbcc1f0f0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512459} {:answer/id #uuid "d7ba38e6-e652-5b50-b3d7-ba917e7a89bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e900ee1-3dca-5910-b252-b7b9299af900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 18\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512433} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ee2384a-f8ed-53d5-a42e-da2c4beee47c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512749}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "67636a56-1e5b-5200-b7f3-14f05ab714df" :question/math-academy-id "q-138640" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 8 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the sample covariance matrix of the data." :question/worked-solution "Recall that  the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{n-1}B{B}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nSo, we first need to compute the mean-deviation form of our observation matrix.\n\nThe sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the sample covariance matrix is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{3-1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 18\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512915 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162095 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc84d72a-b9f3-5f99-aa23-31cfe6910d49" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b7af902-b842-5b29-a228-d25f383a43ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512227} {:answer/id #uuid "4536e172-f637-5139-9267-23d685944188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}18 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512244} {:answer/id #uuid "58969516-8d79-5408-bf8d-22119bd156fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}18 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512305} {:answer/id #uuid "7dacd88f-1a54-51a7-88e9-6306954f67ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512395} {:answer/id #uuid "faa4bf33-0b8b-57e1-99cc-e6c1e2c14038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}9 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512702}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4536e172-f637-5139-9267-23d685944188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}18 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512244} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4dedb56-1543-5c95-9a8b-146642e9b77e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a2f76723-41c1-52ba-a0e5-e2eb590f9ddf" :question/math-academy-id "q-138641" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 13 & 10 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the sample covariance matrix of the data." :question/worked-solution "Recall that  the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{n-1}B{B}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nSo, we first need to compute the mean-deviation form of our observation matrix.\n\nThe sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}30 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the sample covariance matrix is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{3-1}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}18 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
